{"packet_id":"D007-01","doc_id":"D007","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California security deposit cap (AB 12)","requirement":"Landlords generally may charge no more than one month's rent as a security deposit, except small landlords who own only two rental properties of four units or fewer, who may charge up to two months. Deposits must be returned within 21 days of move-out with an itemized statement.","key_value":"1 month's rent; 2 months' rent for qualifying small landlords","coverage_conditions":"All residential tenancies; exception for landlords owning only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total, held by a natural person, family trust, or LLC of natural persons.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"landlords who own only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total, held by a natural person, family trust, or LLC of natural persons","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["Starting July 1, 2024, many landlords may only charge one month's rent for unfurnished and furnished units","Starting July 1, 2024, landlords who own only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total can charge up to two months' rent for furnished and unfurnished units if ownership is held by a natural person, family trust, or limited liability company (LLC) where all members are natural persons"]},"exemptions":"Landlords who own only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total, held by a natural person, family trust, or LLC of natural persons, may charge up to two months' rent.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-07-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"AB 12","quoted_span":"Starting July 1, 2024, many landlords may only charge one month's rent for unfurnished and furnished units","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D007-01","doc_id":"D007","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance security deposit interest","requirement":"Landlords of units covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance must pay tenants interest on their security deposit at the end of each year, and a prorated amount if the tenant moves out before the end of the year.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"other","text":"units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance"}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["For tenancies in units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance, landlords must pay tenants interest on their security deposit at the end of each year and a prorated amount if the tenant moves out before the end of the year."]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.76","quoted_span":"For tenancies in units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance, landlords must pay tenants interest on their security deposit at the end of each year and a prorated amount if the tenant moves out before the end of the year.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
